;; repr/asm's arm64 read level's classes (doc/asm/SPEC.md §8, §10; doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md §4.4, §12, AR1 "the rest classed"): every
;; row of test/asm/roundtrip-results-arm64.edn that does not pass is in the first class whose :match finds its REASON (or whose :ids
;; names it), in goi's format. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :error-test
  :title "an error test rejected"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the test's RUN lines say llvm-mc rejects it (`not llvm-mc`) and repr/asm's reader rejects it too, at the syntax level (a trailing comma, a list `{v0.8b-}`, `;;` as two separators and words, `=())`, `@` without a name, `$` before an equate's end); that the rejection is the test's, with the message fragment its CHECK lines state, is AR2's judge (doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md §4.1 (3), ARS10)"
  :decided "AR1's scope (doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md §12); since AXS96 (a) (2026-11-17) the read goes on after a refused statement and holds each refusal to the test's error lines (:error-misplaced), this class kept for a refusal the reader cannot go on from"
  :match [#"^error-test refused "]}
 {:id :error-misplaced
  :title "an error test's refusal where the test states no error"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "AXS96 (a)'s judge: the reader refuses a statement of an error test at a line none of the test's error CHECK lines names (a [[#@LINE]] place, a NAME.s:N: place, else the statements beside the CHECK line). Not a failure by itself: a test need not state every error llvm-mc reports (FileCheck holds the stated ones), so llvm-mc may refuse the statement too (`;; Exponent too large` in AArch64's ELF syntax is a statement); which of the two is the oracle tier's, by hand"
  :decided "AXS96 (a) (the user, 2026-11-17, round 51)"
  :match [#"^error-test misplaced "]}
 {:id :other-arch
  :title "a test of another target"
  :kind :design
  :why "the test's RUN lines name no AArch64 triple: amd64's crop reads it"
  :decided "ARS1 (a), two crops (the user, 2026-11-09)"
  :match [#"^other-arch "]}
 {:id :not-input
  :title "a test file that is not assembly"
  :kind :design
  :why "the test's RUN lines never give the file itself (%s) to llvm-mc"
  :decided "AR1's scope"
  :match [#"^not-input "]}
]
